.TH qsh-trust-set-role 1  "set-role 0.5.6" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-trust\-set\-role \- Change the trust role of a pinned peer (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0045). The only command that changes the role of a pin that already exists. Takes effect from the peer\*(Aqs next request with no restart: roles are read on every decision, unlike `acl.toml` rows. The role is one of `full`, `exec`, `tunnel`, `read\-only`, `reverse`, `none`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh trust set\-role\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fINAME\fR> <\fIROLE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change the trust role of a pinned peer (`docs/CLI.md` §6.11, ADR\-0045). The only command that changes the role of a pin that already exists. Takes effect from the peer\*(Aqs next request with no restart: roles are read on every decision, unlike `acl.toml` rows. The role is one of `full`, `exec`, `tunnel`, `read\-only`, `reverse`, `none`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
The pinned peer\*(Aqs name
.TP
<\fIROLE\fR>
The new role
.SH VERSION
v0.5.6
